# What a Code agent on each repository is given: where it starts, how it lands, what follows, its limits and the words of its approval.
> code-brief {"name":"openagents"}
< {"ok":true,"schema":"gamebuilder.code.v1","repo":"openagents","github":"OpenAgentsInc/openagents","is":"the engine","from":"origin/main","rules":"AGENTS.md","ends":"pull-request","then":"pin-bump","limits":{"turns":80,"cents":1000},"approval":"confirm","words":["A Code agent is your Claude Code with its normal tools: it can run commands and change files in its own folder, which a Builder cannot. Its commands run as you on this computer; it is told to stay in its folder, and the app refuses its file edits anywhere else.","It works in a fresh git worktree made from origin/main, in a folder GameBuilder makes for it (~/gamebuilder-code), outside the app's own folders and outside any main checkout, and follows the repository's AGENTS.md.","It ends in a pull request at OpenAgentsInc/openagents for a person to merge. It never pushes to main: a hook in its folder refuses that. Without push access there, it pushes its branch to your own fork of the engine on GitHub, which it makes in your name the first time.","After it merges, the pane offers the next job here: a Code agent on the app that moves openagents.lock to the merged commit (scripts/pin.sh bump) with scripts/check.sh passing.","It runs on your own Claude plan, signed in to Claude Code on this computer: never an API key, and no Credits."]}
> code-brief {"name":"gamebuilder"}
< {"ok":true,"schema":"gamebuilder.code.v1","repo":"gamebuilder","github":"OpenAgentsInc/gamebuilder","is":"the app","from":"origin/main","rules":"AGENTS.md","ends":"repository-rules","then":"","limits":{"turns":80,"cents":1000},"approval":"confirm","words":["A Code agent is your Claude Code with its normal tools: it can run commands and change files in its own folder, which a Builder cannot. Its commands run as you on this computer; it is told to stay in its folder, and the app refuses its file edits anywhere else.","It works in a fresh git worktree made from origin/main, in a folder GameBuilder makes for it (~/gamebuilder-code), outside the app's own folders and outside any main checkout, and follows the repository's AGENTS.md.","It lands its work by this repository's own rules (its AGENTS.md): checked with scripts/check.sh and scripts/build.sh, then pushed to main.","It runs on your own Claude plan, signed in to Claude Code on this computer: never an API key, and no Credits."]}
